  #line-at(85.544pt, 337.784pt, "Abstract")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.544pt, 368.024pt, "The success of distributed photovoltaics may be undermining its own future. As solar ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 383.864pt, "penetration increases, electricity prices fall during periods of peak generation, reducing ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 399.704pt, "the value of surplus photovoltaic production. This raises a critical question for the energy ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 415.544pt, "transition: can citizen-led energy systems remain economically viable in electricity ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 431.384pt, "markets increasingly dominated by renewable generation? ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 461.864pt, "Rather than exploring technically optimal but institutionally unrealistic solutions, we ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 477.704pt, "investigate what options remain available to ordinary citizens under current regulatory ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 493.544pt, "and market conditions. Using high-resolution consumption data of a mature rural ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 509.384pt, "community sharing a PV facility among 24 users, providing evidence-based insights into ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 525.224pt, "pathways for long-term sustainability. Key contributions are advanced. First, the analysis ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 541.064pt, "redefines the value proposition of collective energy systems, showing that robust internal ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 556.904pt, "coordination can mobilize participation and investment as effectively as external ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 572.744pt, "subsidies, an insight particularly relevant for contexts facing capital constraints. Second, ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 588.824pt, "the study evaluates alternative energy-sharing mechanisms that move beyond fixed ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 604.664pt, "equity-based allocations. By systematically comparing static, dynamic, and hybrid ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 620.504pt, "models—with and without storage integration—it develops an adaptable framework that ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 636.344pt, "balances fairness and flexibility while aligning with evolving governance needs. ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 666.584pt, "Results show that collective self-consumption generates substantial coordination benefits, ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 682.424pt, "reducing required PV capacity, lowering investment costs, and increasing annual savings ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 698.264pt, "compared with equivalent individually operated systems. Alternative allocation schemes ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 714.104pt, "further improve the distribution of benefits among participants and enhance the utilization ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 729.944pt, "of locally generated electricity, although gains depend on the trade-off between ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 746.024pt, "efficiency, fairness, and governance complexity. By contrast, under current electricity ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 761.864pt, "prices and remuneration schemes, battery storage provides only limited additional ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 777.704pt, "economic value, becoming attractive only under specific market conditions. The findings ")
]

