  #line-at(419.558pt, 347.624pt, ". ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 377.384pt, "The battery storage capacity is shared proportionally among users. Each user optimizes ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 393.224pt, "their own consumption and storage strategy independently, within their allocated capacity ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 409.304pt, "limits. This structure allows for the evaluation of how different production and ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 425.144pt, "consumption profiles influence the individual economic benefits of shared energy storage ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 440.984pt, "in a community setting. ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 470.744pt, "For the battery model, the reported savings represent the reduction in electricity costs ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 486.584pt, "compared to a scenario with a collective photovoltaic (PV) plant but without storage. ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 502.424pt, "These savings are calculated as described in equation 5, where: ")
  #line-at(121.544pt, 532.424pt, "C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(129.548pt, 533.384pt, "baseline")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(155.759pt, 532.424pt, " is the total electricity cost in the scenario with collective PV but without ")
  #line-at(121.544pt, 548.264pt, "battery storage ")
  #line-at(121.544pt, 564.104pt, "C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(129.548pt, 565.064pt, "optimized")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(161.54pt, 564.104pt, " is the total electricity cost in the scenario with both PV and battery ")
  #line-at(121.544pt, 579.944pt, "storage ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.544pt, 610.424pt, "Economic Feasibility and Sensitivity Analysis ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.544pt, 640.664pt, "As a complement to the energy optimization model, an economic evaluation of the ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 656.504pt, "community storage system is carried out by calculating the Internal Rate of Return (IRR), ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 672.344pt, "along with sensitivity analyses to understand how outcomes change under different ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 688.184pt, "market scenarios  -uncertainty in prices (±30 to 100%) and battery costs (±50%)- ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 717.944pt, "The economic analysis is based on the annual savings that the community would achieve, ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 733.784pt, "according to the model results. These data are used to project cash flows over a 15-year ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 749.864pt, "period, which approximately corresponds to the useful life of a lithium-ion battery system ")
]

// arXiv source page 16
#original-page(595.276pt, 841.89pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.824pt, 804.344pt, "16 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 82.664pt, "in stationary applications. The initial investment is estimated based on a baseline cost of ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 98.744pt, "€250/kWh, applied to the system’s total usable capacity. ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 128.504pt, "The IRR is calculated using the irr() function from the numpy-financial library, which ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 144.344pt, "determines the discount rate that makes the net present value of cash flows equal to zero. ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 160.184pt, "In this analysis, the initial cash flow corresponds to the total cost of the storage system (a ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 176.024pt, "negative value), followed by positive annual flows equivalent to the energy savings ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 191.864pt, "generated. No residual value is included at the end of the period, making this a ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 207.944pt, "conservative and cautious profitability estimate. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(103.544pt, 238.184pt, "3.")
  #line-at(121.544pt, 238.184pt, "Results and discussion ")
  #line-at(103.544pt, 254.024pt, "3.1")
  #line-at(122.544pt, 254.024pt, "Individual self-consumption approach ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.544pt, 284.264pt, "The purpose of this comparison is not to evaluate future decisions, but to establish a ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 300.104pt, "reference scenario against which the value generated by collective coordination can be ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 315.944pt, "quantified. The individual self-consumption case therefore serves as a counterfactual ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 331.784pt, "benchmark representing a fragmented operation of the same users and demand profiles. ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 355.784pt, "In this first simulation, the PV installation for each user was sized according to their ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 371.624pt, "individual annual electricity demand. The system design was based on the technical ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 387.464pt, "specifications of the PV modules used in the real project, ensuring both realism and ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 403.304pt, "consistency. Each system's capacity was adjusted in discrete steps corresponding to whole ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 419.144pt, "units of these modules, resulting in technically feasible system sizes. The performance ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 434.984pt, "and financial results for these individually sized PV systems are summarised in Table 3.  ")
]

