  #line-at(55.544pt, 114.584pt, "75 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 130.424pt, "attractiveness of collective self-consumption even under current electricity market ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 130.424pt, "76 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 146.264pt, "conditions. Savings are around 55% of the variable electricity bill and about 20% higher ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 146.264pt, "77 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 162.104pt, "than the combined savings achieved by the 24 individual systems (€16,956 versus ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 162.104pt, "78 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 177.944pt, "€13,077). ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 177.944pt, "79 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 207.944pt, "Part of this advantage comes from the diversity of consumption profiles. When users ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 207.944pt, "80 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 223.784pt, "share generation, energy that would otherwise be exported to the grid can often be ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 223.784pt, "81 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 239.624pt, "consumed by another member of the community. As a result, more locally generated ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 239.624pt, "82 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 255.464pt, "electricity is used on-site and less value is lost through low export prices. ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 255.464pt, "83 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 285.224pt, "It should also be noted that these calculations only consider energy-related costs. ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 285.224pt, "84 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 301.304pt, "Contracted power charges, metering fees and taxes were not included. In practice, ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 301.304pt, "85 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 317.144pt, "community members may achieve additional savings by reducing contracted power levels ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 317.144pt, "86 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 332.984pt, "and benefiting from the regulatory framework for collective self-consumption. Actual ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 332.984pt, "87 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 348.824pt, "economic benefits are therefore likely to be somewhat higher than those reported here. ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 348.824pt, "88 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 378.584pt, "Beyond the financial results, collective self-consumption also offers practical advantages. ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 378.584pt, "89 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 394.424pt, "A single grid connection simplifies administration and permitting, maintenance can be ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 394.424pt, "90 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 410.504pt, "managed collectively, and the installation retains flexibility to accommodate future ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 410.504pt, "91 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 426.344pt, "members or new loads such as electric vehicle charging. ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 426.344pt, "92 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 456.104pt, "Most importantly, these results show that a significant share of the value generated by the ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 456.104pt, "93 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 471.944pt, "community comes from coordination rather than from photovoltaic generation alone. ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 471.944pt, "94 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 487.784pt, "When users share a common installation, differences in their consumption patterns allow ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 487.784pt, "95 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 503.624pt, "locally generated electricity to be used more efficiently. Energy that would otherwise be ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 503.624pt, "96 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 519.704pt, "exported to the grid by one participant can often be consumed by another, increasing self-")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 519.704pt, "97 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 535.544pt, "consumption and reducing overall costs. ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 535.544pt, "98 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 565.304pt, "Although exploring this effect in detail is beyond the scope of this paper, we propose to ")
  #line-at(55.544pt, 565.304pt, "99 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 581.144pt, "define the load-profile complementarity or complementarity index to understand benefits ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 581.144pt, "100 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 596.984pt, "to share consumption that could be obtained by users.  In simple terms, this indicator, ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 596.984pt, "101 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 613.064pt, "defined in equation 12, would describe how well the demand patterns of different users ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 613.064pt, "102 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 628.904pt, "fit together. It is calculated as the difference between the PV energy consumed under ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 628.904pt, "103 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 644.744pt, "aggregated operation and the sum of PV energy self-consumed by each user operating ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 644.744pt, "104 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 660.584pt, "independently, normalized by the total PV generation. Higher values would indicate ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 660.584pt, "105 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 676.424pt, "greater complementarity among demand profiles and a stronger potential for collective ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 676.424pt, "106 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 692.264pt, "self-consumption benefits. ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 692.264pt, "107 ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
