#original-page(595.276pt, 841.89pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.824pt, 804.344pt, "28 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 82.664pt, "sharing models within renewable energy communities. The marginal contribution is ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 82.664pt, "239 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 98.744pt, "defined in equation 7 and results are shown in Table 6. ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 98.744pt, "240 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 128.504pt, "This method is implemented through a set of fixed allocation shares that remain constant ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 128.504pt, "241 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 144.344pt, "throughout the year. Under this allocation scheme, the community reaches a SCR of ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 144.344pt, "242 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 160.184pt, "60.1% and a SSR of 55.4%. Compared with the current equity-based allocation, the SCR ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 160.184pt, "243 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 176.024pt, "increases by 10.9 percentage points, highlighting the value of considering each ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 176.024pt, "244 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 191.864pt, "participant’s contribution to collective performance rather than relying solely on ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 191.864pt, "245 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 207.944pt, "investment shares. Although the MC approach does not achieve the performance of the ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 207.944pt, "246 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 223.784pt, "dynamic allocation models explored above, it provides a substantial improvement while ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 223.784pt, "247 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 239.624pt, "also remaining compatible with the fixed-share requirements of current regulation, and it ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 239.624pt, "248 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 255.464pt, "could be easily to calculate for lay citizens. ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 255.464pt, "249 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 285.224pt, "From a technical perspective, the MC model better aligns incentives with system ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 285.224pt, "250 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 301.304pt, "performance and can therefore be considered a fair allocation mechanism from an ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 301.304pt, "251 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 317.144pt, "operational standpoint. However, its implementation may be socially challenging in ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 317.144pt, "252 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 332.984pt, "established energy communities. Participants who financed a significant share of the ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 332.984pt, "253 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 348.824pt, "installation may perceive a substantial reduction in their allocation rights despite having ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 348.824pt, "254 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 364.664pt, "assumed a larger financial risk during the project's development. Consequently, although ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 364.664pt, "255 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 380.504pt, "the MC approach improves efficiency, it may create governance tensions if introduced ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 380.504pt, "256 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 396.344pt, "abruptly. ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 396.344pt, "257 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(103.544pt, 426.824pt, "3.2.2.4")
  #line-at(157.544pt, 426.824pt, "Set allocation based on investment and Marginal Contribution to ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.544pt, 426.824pt, "258 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(157.544pt, 442.424pt, "Profit (MC) ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.544pt, 442.424pt, "259 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 472.904pt, "This hybrid model was developed to address the main limitation of the previous ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 472.904pt, "260 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 488.744pt, "approaches. While the equity-based model recognizes the financial commitment made by ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 488.744pt, "261 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 504.584pt, "participants, it ignores their actual contribution to the efficient use of community energy.  ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 504.584pt, "262 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 520.424pt, "Conversely, the MC model rewards operational value creation but may disregard the ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 520.424pt, "263 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 536.264pt, "investments that enabled the project in the first place. The hybrid approach combines both ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 536.264pt, "264 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 552.104pt, "perspectives by allocating 50% of the shares according to ownership and 50% according ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 552.104pt, "265 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 567.944pt, "to marginal contribution. The objective is not to maximize technical performance alone, ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 567.944pt, "266 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 583.784pt, "but to provide a practical transition pathway for existing energy communities seeking to ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 583.784pt, "267 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 599.864pt, "improve efficiency without undermining previously established investment agreements ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 599.864pt, "268 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 615.704pt, ". ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 615.704pt, "269 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 631.544pt, "The hybrid model provides a compromise between efficiency and stability. As shown in ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 631.544pt, "270 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 647.384pt, "Figure 2 and Table 6, the resulting allocations remain relatively close to the current ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 647.384pt, "271 ")
