  #line-at(49.544pt, 599.864pt, "391 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 629.624pt, "For mature energy communities, the flexible model with surplus sharing seems to provide ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 629.624pt, "392 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 645.464pt, "the most balanced approach. It keeps most of the effectiveness and savings from flexible ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 645.464pt, "393 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 661.304pt, "allocation while ensuring a clear connection between investments and the distribution of ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 661.304pt, "394 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 677.144pt, "benefits. ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 677.144pt, "395 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 707.144pt, "The idea of setting shares based on past hourly usage might be seen as a risk by members ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 707.144pt, "396 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 722.984pt, "of the community. In Spain, users currently have access to only two years of past usage ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 722.984pt, "397 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 738.824pt, "data, and yearly changes of up to 9,3% were noted in this study. As a result, allocation ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 738.824pt, "398 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 754.664pt, "figures based on previous habits cannot ensure that future usage patterns will be ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 754.664pt, "399 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 770.504pt, "accurately reflected. However, this limitation is somewhat eased by the rules, which ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 770.504pt, "400 ")
]

// arXiv source page 33
#original-page(595.276pt, 841.89pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.824pt, 804.344pt, "33 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 82.664pt, "permit hourly allocation figures shared with the DSO to be updated up to four times a ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 82.664pt, "401 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 98.744pt, "year. Thus, historical-demand allocation should not be seen as a fixed rule, but as a ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 98.744pt, "402 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 114.584pt, "flexible system that can change as usage patterns evolve.  ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 114.584pt, "403 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 144.344pt, "Like the idea of a Typical Meteorological Year used in PV modelling, future applications ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 144.344pt, "404 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 160.184pt, "could rely on typical demand profiles created from longer usage records, lessening the ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 160.184pt, "405 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 176.024pt, "impact of unusual years and enhancing the strength of the allocation process. ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 176.024pt, "406 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 206.024pt, "The MCP approach provides an attractive mechanism for rewarding value creation and ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 206.024pt, "407 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 221.864pt, "operational contribution. However, technical and economic optimality should not be ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 221.864pt, "408 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 237.704pt, "confused with social optimality. By explicitly linking benefits to each member’s ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 237.704pt, "409 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 253.544pt, "contribution to collective profitability, MCP may implicitly classify some participants as ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 253.544pt, "410 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 269.384pt, "net contributors and others as net beneficiaries. Although economically efficient, such ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 269.384pt, "411 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 285.224pt, "differentiation may conflict with the cooperative principles that underpin many citizen-")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 285.224pt, "412 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 301.304pt, "led energy communities and may reduce social acceptance if not accompanied by ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 301.304pt, "413 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 317.144pt, "transparent governance and participatory decision-making processes. ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 317.144pt, "414 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 346.904pt, "Under these conditions, the hybrid 50% Equity–50% MCP scheme emerges as an ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 346.904pt, "415 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 362.744pt, "attractive transition strategy for established communities seeking to move progressively ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 362.744pt, "416 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 378.584pt, "from investment-based allocation towards performance-based mechanisms. By ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 378.584pt, "417 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 394.424pt, "combining investment recognition with incentives linked to value creation, it mitigates ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 394.424pt, "418 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 410.504pt, "many of the governance challenges associated with pure MCP schemes while improving ")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 410.504pt, "419 ")
  #line-at(85.544pt, 426.344pt, "the efficiency of energy distribution.")
  #line-at(49.544pt, 426.344pt, "420 ")
]

